# --- Benchmark scratch (2.7 GB, all of it local) ----------------------------
# bench/ is where the whisper accuracy comparison was run. It holds ggml model
# weights, a Python venv, synthetic `say`-generated test clips, and a real
# recording of a real class. None of it belongs in a repo: the weights and venv
# are re-downloadable, and the recording is other people's voices.
bench/

# --- Recordings, transcripts, notes -----------------------------------------
# Nothing this system produces is source. Lecture audio and its transcripts are
# recordings of identifiable people; the note vault is personal coursework.
# The real vault lives on the PC (%USERPROFILE%\Notables), but keep these
# patterns so a stray copy can never be staged by accident.
Recordings/
Outbox/
Vault/
Notes/
Transcripts/
Captures/
Course Materials/
inbox/
_index.json
_courses.json
*.m4a
*.mp3
*.wav
*.aiff
*.aac
*.caf
*.mov
*.whisper

# --- Machine-local config ----------------------------------------------------
# Tailnet addresses and hostnames stay out of git. notables.local holds
# NOTABLES_PC_HOST=<ip or MagicDNS name>; build.sh, deploy-server.sh and the MCP
# bridge read it.
notables.local

# --- Credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
# The shared bearer token and the Canvas session cookie live in ~/.notables/,
# outside the repo. These patterns are belt and braces.
.env
.env.*
.notables/
*token*.txt
canvas-session.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.entitlements.local

# --- Model weights and caches ------------------------------------------------
*.bin
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
.notables-models/
.notables-venv/

